+
+// recalculateOverallState determines the overall state of the process from
+// the state of its components. The overall state is degraded if any of the
+// components is degraded, recovering if any of the components is recovering,
+// starting if any of the components hasn't started yet and ok only when all
+// of the components are ok. The priority order is: degraded > recovering >
+// starting > ok. The caller is expected to hold f.mu.
+func (f *processState) recalculateOverallState() {
+	if len(f.components) == 0 {
+		// No components have reported their state yet.
+		f.updateStateGauge()
